course: dictionary
lesson: 14699
title: Primitive: simple and early
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Primitive means very simple and basic, not advanced. A primitive tool is one made in a simple way, with few parts and no modern technology. «The early people used a primitive axe made of stone.» The clue is made of stone, which is simple, so primitive fits.
explain: Primitive can also mean from an early stage of development, long ago. «Scientists studied primitive life forms found in very old rocks.» Life forms in very old rocks must be from an early time, so primitive means early and basic. Try your meaning in the sentence: does basic and early still make sense? Then it fits.
explain: Be careful. An old, unfair use of primitive described whole peoples as less advanced. This is hurtful and wrong, so do not use it about people. When you meet primitive, read the words around it to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: Primitive means very simple, basic and not advanced.
fact: «Primitive» can also mean from an early stage of development, long ago.
fact: In art, «primitive» can describe a simple, untrained-looking style of painting.
fact: Similar words: basic, simple. The opposite is advanced.
fact: Calling people primitive is seen as unfair and rude today, so never use it that way.
exercise: «The cavemen made a primitive tool from a sharp stone.» What does primitive mean here? | *Very simple and basic | Made of gold | Painted in bright colours | Brand new and high-tech
exercise: «Scientists studied primitive life forms found in very old rocks.» What does primitive suggest? | *From an early stage, long ago | Too expensive to buy | Built only last year | Loud and noisy
exercise: Ella says, «The campsite toilets were primitive, with no water and just a hole in the ground.» What does she mean? | Full of gold | Friendly and welcoming | Very clean and modern | *Basic and not advanced
test: «The early farmers used primitive ploughs made of wood.» What does primitive mean? | Very modern | Painted with bright colours | Made of glass | *Simple and basic
test: Which word is closest in meaning to primitive? | Modern | Advanced | Clever | *Basic
exam: What does primitive most nearly mean in «a primitive tool made of stone»? | *Basic and simple | Shiny | Heavy | Advanced
